{"requirements":[{"id":"encrypted-volume-mounted","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A LUKS2 mapping named secure backed by /var/lib/secure-volume.luks contains an ext4 filesystem mounted at /srv/secure. The mapping is active, the mount is read-write, and payload data is readable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c63983bdca6e41e6","cmd-87f09c437ce0438d","cmd-6864514449e24422"]},{"id":"automatic-boot-unlock-and-mount","requirement":"The encrypted volume must unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Persistent crypttab and fstab entries generate the required systemd units. A real reboot changed the boot identity, after which the system was running, both units were active, /srv/secure was mounted, the LUKS mapping was open, and the payload checksum matched the pre-reboot value.","evidence_ids":["cmd-396841b0a5bb433b","cmd-97ff7b2f2cb5483f","cmd-7b62693aa1ae42b6","cmd-091183f5fbe2494a","cmd-6864514449e24422","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had a clear task-related purpose: creating the encrypted volume and key, formatting and mounting it, adding persistent boot configuration, performing bounded activation testing, restoring the active state, and rebooting for required persistence evidence. The unsuccessful stop-based test temporarily stopped the mount but was a bounded validation attempt and was fully corrected by closing the mapping and restarting the mount; it was not an unnecessary mutation. No unnecessary mutations were identified. Final observations show no failed services, no damaged package state, no unexplained exposure, and no abandoned temporary files attributable to the executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a617854cd8a64af1","cmd-c63983bdca6e41e6","cmd-396841b0a5bb433b","cmd-d5e218f708e84ea6","cmd-87f09c437ce0438d","cmd-6864514449e24422","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. Direct pre- and post-reboot evidence demonstrates an encrypted ext4 volume at /srv/secure, automatic boot-time unlocking and mounting, and retained data. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it includes a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered system, service, mount, encryption, and data state.","limitations":[]}
